    "report_preview": "# Summary\nThe Pastrovići clan (also known as Petrovčići) represents a pivotal noble lineage in Montenegrin history, deeply intertwined with the defense, governance, and cultural development of Budva and the Bay of Kotor region. Emerging from medieval Slavic settlement patterns, the clan migrated to the coastal area during the 15th–16th centuries, establishing themselves as key actors in Venetian-administered politics and later Montenegrin tribal leadership. Their legacy is defined by strategic fortifications, influential voivodes who shaped regional defense and administration, and a socio-political role that bridged coastal nobility with inland Orthodox leadership. Today, their enduring presence is preserved through historical landmarks, genealogical traditions, and active cultural heritage efforts that continue to shape Montenegrin identity.\n\n## Origins and Early Migration History"
  },
